danu (1.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The open set moves: Ctrl and a double-click on a square opens it, the
    set moved onto it; Alt and an arrow moves it a square west, east, north
    or south (View menu, rebindable).
  * Windows: built with the hdf5 MSYS2's GDAL was built against, pinned
    until MSYS2 builds GDAL again (#235).
  * Server: danu-backup prunes the data drop's kept copies weekly - those
    older than DROP_KEEP_DAYS (90), each square's newest kept whatever its
    age. python3 -m danu.drop.store prune, by hand.

