 -- Lee Kindness <wangi@opengeofiction.net>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0100

danu (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The surface is danu.surface.build, the code the editor runs, rather than
    the shell pipeline's own stages: the squares read and nothing else, water
    from the squares, the sea mask's seeds dropped where their step crosses a
    coastline, and isofill through its library where the raster fits.
    danu-build-zone keeps what only a publisher needs.
  * Depends on isofill 0.12.0 or later: the library is checked for the
    version this speaks to, and 0.12.0's second pass is exact out of core.

 -- Lee Kindness <wangi@opengeofiction.net>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:45:00 +0100

danu (0.1.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop --no-start from the soak units. An upgrade stopped a running soak
    timer and never started it again, so a night went missing with nothing to
    show for it. deb-systemd-invoke will not start a disabled or static unit,
    so a fresh install is unaffected.

 -- Lee Kindness <wangi@opengeofiction.net>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:45:00 +0000

danu (0.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add danu-soak, which writes the limit file danu-build already honours so a
    night's run rebuilds two zones for real rather than finding nothing
    changed. Zones are taken in sorted order from a cursor, and it runs on a
    budget of nights so a soak stops on its own.
  * The soak timer is installed but not enabled: forcing rebuilds is a test,
    not what a fresh install should start doing. The soak service carries no
    [Install] at all, so enabling it by hand cannot pull it into default.target
    and queue a rebuild at every boot.

